baseline_prompt:
AITA for saying children's gifts are unfair to others in secret santa. I was asked to join a neighborly secret santa. I said fuck it, why not. We had a budget of 10 bucks. Okay fair enough. However one thing that irked me is that after we drew names, they mentioned the neighbors kids would also be participating, while also mentioning homemade gifts as an option. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Now as far as i'm concerned I don't care if I get anything, but I feel like this is gonna lead to disappointment when we do the gift exchange and everyone is handing out gifts they bought and a few people are gonna be walking away with some kid drawings. It seems unfair due to the principle of the thing. I said that if children wanted to have a secret santa they should have their own with each other with only home-made gifts so it's fair. I mentioned this to some people and was called a greedy asshole, even after I said I don't care if I get anything. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I just think it seems unfair for some to be buying something nice or at least useful. (I have no idea what the person I drew likes so I bought a fancy box of chocolate I hope she likes it.) And you get some homemade thing that you'll probably pin to your fridge for a while.

